# CODEOWNERS — IDC pathway-integrity protected surfaces (spec §2.3).
#
# The ruleset (.github/rulesets/idc-pathway-integrity.json) sets require_code_owner_review, which
# only binds a reviewer once a CODEOWNERS file names each protected surface. ALL ELEVEN surface
# classes the pathway check protects must have an owner here so a PR cannot strip the governance
# machinery without a code-owner's review: the four original classes (workflow, hook, validation,
# receipt), the three governance-of-governance classes (the deterministic checker, the ownership
# checker, the ruleset directory), CODEOWNERS itself, and the three enforcement scripts (the Path
# Gate, the git backstop, the build-receipt minter). scripts/idc_ruleset_check.py --repo-root
# deterministically refuses a ruleset whose protected surfaces are not all owned, and the class list
# it enforces (SURFACE_CLASSES) is checked BOTH WAYS against the ruleset's protected_surfaces — so
# this header cannot drift from the enforced set without a governance lane going red.

# Workflow surface — the version-pinned pathway workflow and any other CI that gates merges.
/.github/workflows/ @llamallamaredpajama

# Hook surface — the Path Gate / interlock / entry / stop hooks that enforce off-path denial.
/scripts/hooks/ @llamallamaredpajama

# Validation surface — the frozen build validation contract.
/scripts/idc_validation_contract.py @llamallamaredpajama

# Receipt surface — the receipt integrity checker.
/scripts/idc_receipt_check.py @llamallamaredpajama

# The deterministic checker and the ruleset itself are load-bearing governance too.
/scripts/idc_pathway_check.py @llamallamaredpajama
# The OWNERSHIP checker — the script that decides whether every protected surface is owned. It was
# the one piece of governance machinery that governed everything except itself: an unreviewed PR
# could weaken the checker that enforces code-owner review and the weakening would certify clean.
/scripts/idc_ruleset_check.py @llamallamaredpajama

# The ENFORCEMENT scripts the spec names as blocking surfaces (§2.2 evidence leg, §5 row T3). They
# were claimed code-owner-protected while nobody owned them and no catch-all rule existed — the same
# defect as the ownership checker above, one file over. The Path Gate decides every mutation; the git
# backstop is the ONLY gate the Codex and Pi runtimes get; the build receipt is the evidence artifact
# Build closes against.
/scripts/idc_path_gate.py @llamallamaredpajama
/scripts/idc_git_path_gate.py @llamallamaredpajama
/scripts/idc_build_receipt.py @llamallamaredpajama

/.github/rulesets/ @llamallamaredpajama
/.github/CODEOWNERS @llamallamaredpajama
